  "query_preview": "Highs once again top out near or just above 100 degrees \nacross the area today, with low to mid 90s in and around the higher \nterrain. Lows tonight bottom out in the low-to-mid 70s for most. \nSimilar to yesterday, isolated to scattered showers and \nthunderstorms are expected to develop this afternoon and evening. \nWhile the best chances (20-40%) will be south and west of the Pecos \nRiver (especially in the higher terrain), low chances (10-20%) are \nmaintained elsewhere thanks to lingering moisture and lift on the \nwestern edge of Edouard's remnants.\n\nEven though ridging continues to build westward Saturday, relatively \nlower heights over our area yield temperatures a degree or two \ncooler than today's. Highs in the mid-to-upper 90s will be \ncommonplace, with 100 degree temperatures becoming more confined to \nthe river valleys. Lows Saturday night end up similar to tonight's. \nIsolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms will develop again \ntomorrow afternoon and evening, but this time will remain mainly \nsouth and west of the Pecos, with a few sneaking into the western \nPermian Basin (20-40% chances for these locations). For both today \nand tomorrow, storms that develop may produce heavy rainfall, strong \nwinds, and frequent lightning.\n\nSprang",
